        "is_free": false,
        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Commit. Dodge. Strike.</strong><br>In <i>The Elomont Raider</i>, you <strong>move instantly with WASD</strong>, but <strong>once you attack, you can’t move until the action finishes</strong>—and enemies follow the same rule.<br>It’s a classic arcade-style challenge built around timing, openings, and clean execution.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Key Features</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Commit-to-attack combat</strong>: attacking locks movement—choose your moment, then make it count.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Simple controls, real depth</strong>: left click for basic attack, right click for a special skill—each weapon has two forms.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Readable patterns (not full-screen chaos)</strong>: projectiles and AoE threats that reward positioning and patience.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Retro fantasy vibes</strong>: goblins, demons, and diabolical monsters with classic round-bullet visuals.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Nostalgia collectibles</strong>: open chests to find “memory icons” like game consoles, comics, sneakers, and trophies—small reminders of better days.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Arcade-first pacing</strong>: quick retries, tight stages, and boss fights that test your timing.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Background</strong><br>A modern adult, exhausted by life, is pulled into a strange magical world—one that feels like the fantasies he dreamed of as a kid.<br>Fight forward, recover fragments of memory, and find your way back.</p>",
        "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Commit. Dodge. Strike.</strong><br>In <i>The Elomont Raider</i>, you <strong>move instantly with WASD</strong>, but <strong>once you attack, you can’t move until the action finishes</strong>—and enemies follow the same rule.<br>It’s a classic arcade-style challenge built around timing, openings, and clean execution.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Key Features</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Commit-to-attack combat</strong>: attacking locks movement—choose your moment, then make it count.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Simple controls, real depth</strong>: left click for basic attack, right click for a special skill—each weapon has two forms.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Readable patterns (not full-screen chaos)</strong>: projectiles and AoE threats that reward positioning and patience.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Retro fantasy vibes</strong>: goblins, demons, and diabolical monsters with classic round-bullet visuals.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Nostalgia collectibles</strong>: open chests to find “memory icons” like game consoles, comics, sneakers, and trophies—small reminders of better days.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Arcade-first pacing</strong>: quick retries, tight stages, and boss fights that test your timing.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Background</strong><br>A modern adult, exhausted by life, is pulled into a strange magical world—one that feels like the fantasies he dreamed of as a kid.<br>Fight forward, recover fragments of memory, and find your way back.</p>",
        "short_description": "A retro top-down arcade shooter where every attack is a commitment. Move fast, lock in to cast, dodge patterns, and strike when the opening appears.",
